This file is NOT output of the current code. It records what
scripts/test_request_construction_controls.sh printed on its FIRST run, while it
was RED -- before the three unprotected fixes below had controls.

It is kept for the same reason samples/gate-evidence/check_figures.RED.out is: a
gate whose first run is green tells you nothing about whether it can fail. These
three were real gaps, found by the gate on itself:

  C1  framing defined as the remainder -- equivalent ALONE, and the enabler of a
      tautological coverage check when combined with a narrowed field split. The
      case was rewritten to revert BOTH, which is the implementation somebody
      would really write, and a new control now requires the split to NAME every
      top-level field.
  C12 the mutation recorded an EMPTY header dict, so it leaked nothing and the
      control was right not to fire. record() now takes the header MAPPING and
      keeps names only, so the leaky revert is a one-word change and is caught.
  C13 keep-alive SSE was neutralised by a later close_connection assignment, so
      the stream still terminated. The case now reverts that line.

--- verbatim first run ---
REVERT-EACH-FIX GATE (request construction) -- 13 cases
Each reverts one fix to the simpler code somebody would really write; a control must turn RED.

baseline: the unmutated copies of both files PASS their self-tests, so a RED below is caused by the mutation

C1-framing-definitional            GREEN -- COVERAGE GAP
C2-coverage-three-columns          RED   -- FAIL  coverage invariant did not hold on a clean fixture
C3-probe-counts-as-turn            RED   -- FAIL  probe-only capture -> exit 4, probes=0
C4-unknown-field-ignored           RED   -- FAIL  unknown field -> exit 0, unknown=[]
C5-metadata-billed-as-input        RED   -- FAIL  provider-metadata split wrong: meta=759 reported=759
C6-openai-system-as-conversation   RED   -- FAIL  protocol normalisation failed: anth system=13 oai system=0, msgs 1/2
C7-one-assumed-model               RED   -- FAIL  per-model grouping wrong: ['model-a']
C8-corrupt-line-skipped            RED   -- FAIL  a corrupt capture was measured anyway: exit 0
C9-claims-whitespace-exact         RED   -- FAIL  the gate fired on reflowed prose: PUBLISHED-CLAIM CHECK against /tmp/ari-mrc-selft
C10-faithfulness-always-ok         RED   -- FAIL  faithfulness passed against a different capture
C11-empty-reference-passes         RED   -- FAIL  a probe-only reference was treated as checkable
C12-recorder-logs-header-values    GREEN -- COVERAGE GAP
C13-recorder-keepalive-sse         GREEN -- COVERAGE GAP

FAILED -- 3 of 13 fixes are unprotected:
  C1-framing-definitional: reverting it changes nothing the self-test can see
    what the revert costs: defining JSON framing as `whole - sum(fields)` instead of predicting it from the structure. It looks equivalent and makes the coverage invariant TAUTOLOGICAL: framing silently absorbs any field missing from the split, so the check can never fail and the instrument reports a payload smaller than the one that was sent.
  C12-recorder-logs-header-values: reverting it changes nothing the self-test can see
    what the revert costs: recording header VALUES as well as names. The Authorization / x-api-key value of a misconfigured run then lands in a capture file whose whole purpose is to be publishable.
  C13-recorder-keepalive-sse: reverting it changes nothing the self-test can see
    what the revert costs: answering an event stream under keep-alive. With no Content-Length the client cannot tell the body ended and blocks until its own timeout -- and a recorder that hangs the client reads as a client that never sent anything.
exit=1
